# Third-party corpora. The bulk payloads stay local — upstream owns them, and a
# clone pinned to a commit is more recoverable than a copy vendored into our
# history. research/README.md IS tracked and names every expected clone with its
# URL and pinned commit, so losing one is never silent (2026-08-10: macula-greek
# and morphgnt-sblgnt had both vanished from readers-gnt with no trace, because a
# blanket `research/` ignore leaves nothing behind to notice their absence).
#
# Our own analysis does NOT belong here. It goes in the numbered tiers — evidence
# in 2-evidence/, scripts in 5-machinery/ — where git can diff and recover it.
research/*
!research/README.md

# Pre-publication strategy, methodology canon, session artifacts (Dropbox-junctioned)
# Private material stays local. The README stub is the exception and IS
# tracked, so the folder's purpose and layout survive even though its
# contents cannot. A bare `private/` cannot be negated into -- git will not
# descend into an ignored directory -- so the contents are ignored instead.
/private/*
!/private/README.md

# Machine-specific Claude Code permissions (cross-project paths shouldn't be public)
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# Claude Code scheduled-task runtime artifact (transient, machine-local)
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Stray Python install detritus (Windows Python installer drops these)
Python/
python_install_*.log

# Captured cascade-run output (one-off redirects from apply_specs / apply_validators
# / refresh_book runs; not editorial source-of-truth)
refresh_log*.txt
apply_*_log*.txt
cascade_log*.txt

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editor
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Obsidian-generated default file (not editorial content)
Welcome.md

# Local environment
.env

# Generated alignment data (machine-generated; re-run run_eflomal_alignment.py)
data/alignment/

# Generated audit-trail reports (per-run apply diffs + per-book quality scorecards;
# accumulate forever, regeneratable on demand, not editorial source-of-truth)
data/reports/
